<article class="env-lemma" id="9655">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9655">Lemma <span data-tag="9655">4.4.5.11</span>.</a> The inclusion $\Idem \subseteq \Idem ^{+}$ is a cofinal map of simplicial sets. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Theorem <a href="/tag/974D" data-tag="974D">4.1.3.1</a>, it will suffice to prove that the simplicial sets $\Idem _{x/}$ and $\Idem _{y/}$ are weakly contractible. The simplicial set $\Idem _{x/}$ is an $\infty $-category with an initial object, and therefore weakly contractible. The projection $\Idem _{y/} \rightarrow \Idem $ is an isomorphism, and $\Idem $ is weakly contractible by Lemma <a href="/tag/A3D9" data-tag="A3D9">4.4.5.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>